    <Folder>
      <name>Locations</name>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Alchemax Tower</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR5ib89OCKPo6JU9jMpK-SKJls9dEzrpVWTNhpOlwuouSeIRIkthcjsb3jrP4HgqmYmaBjylMVxZEiezSeFXJMuMhpLtC2nLIREjchhvGF_R92oJ4fzhMwrjEwr868QwCftbe8anLWDAoCgKjgKZnLINlITnYTep2RX8efY9-aXrrmNQ_BSqmM8-IFpQTOX15gCx9dk?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Description: Former Oscorp tower, rebranded Alchemax after the merger between Oscorp, Allan Chemical, and Horizon Labs.<br>Notes: Will Sliney’s multiple establishing shots of the Alchemax Building from the Spider-Man 2099 (2014) series place it next to the Carnegie Hall Tower in the position of the Park Hyatt Building.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1769-FF5252-labelson</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Description">
            <value>Former Oscorp tower, rebranded Alchemax after the merger between Oscorp, Allan Chemical, and Horizon Labs.</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Notes">
            <value>Will Sliney’s multiple establishing shots of the Alchemax Building from the Spider-Man 2099 (2014) series place it next to the Carnegie Hall Tower in the position of the Park Hyatt Building.</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value><![CDATA[https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR5ib89OCKPo6JU9jMpK-SKJls9dEzrpVWTNhpOlwuouSeIRIkthcjsb3jrP4HgqmYmaBjylMVxZEiezSeFXJMuMhpLtC2nLIREjchhvGF_R92oJ4fzhMwrjEwr868QwCftbe8anLWDAoCgKjgKZnLINlITnYTep2RX8efY9-aXrrmNQ_BSqmM8-IFpQTOX15gCx9dk?authuser=0&fife=s16383]]></value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            -73.9790537,40.7656655,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Alias Investigations</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR62BlqB9NQtQEPTt0oeClqhkvieeTc2thR88mN6nhlaGuVh-cyIdRyXLQ3i3RH9EJqN1FPifpQqSaMZncdIX1os41-jJgsk_QgJQoQmZW84SZAeiU6zEc0zu5cY5ZuBiUwJOUpHDDd7falvW2ieLXHQXiSt7q2H7v6Jl9TfK-wmEvMqYCsAKOx5FMi4PkM11nlxKks?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Description: Jessica Jones’ private investigation office<br>Notes: There was little indication of the location of Jessica Jones’ office until Kelly Thompson’s Jessica Jones: Purple Daughter (2019) arc revealed it was in Hell’s Kitchen (as it was in the Netflix television series). Beyond that, this placemark is merely dropped in a part of the city that looks resembles Jessica’s neighborhood (which has changed a bit over the years). It's also above a bar.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1594-757575-labelson</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Description">
            <value>Jessica Jones’ private investigation office</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Notes">
            <value><![CDATA[There was little indication of the location of Jessica Jones’ office until Kelly Thompson’s Jessica Jones: Purple Daughter (2019) arc revealed it was in Hell’s Kitchen (as it was in the Netflix television series). Beyond that, this placemark is merely dropped in a part of the city that looks resembles Jessica’s neighborhood (which has changed a bit over the years). It's also above a bar.]]></value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value><![CDATA[https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR62BlqB9NQtQEPTt0oeClqhkvieeTc2thR88mN6nhlaGuVh-cyIdRyXLQ3i3RH9EJqN1FPifpQqSaMZncdIX1os41-jJgsk_QgJQoQmZW84SZAeiU6zEc0zu5cY5ZuBiUwJOUpHDDd7falvW2ieLXHQXiSt7q2H7v6Jl9TfK-wmEvMqYCsAKOx5FMi4PkM11nlxKks?authuser=0&fife=s16383]]></value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            -73.9936185,40.7567603,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name><![CDATA[Ancient One's Temple]]></name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR7wuTm_JoK9gnQJ-HnWDUVrq5Ls--o-dksbqOoJ79jDfb2xnwYoGUytyyJUELHq_IGuBNltqXzVEws7GsLyxj-dhrjm8lx2AvRjO0y4xY5Rp8IxWGI_pdNLbY-LCHuDiyvsKldo6SCN4rfdhECT8mJhdsklzcrl2rJiGe7iyOCNgRsGG6dgPHQEmpp16sgwR1w44x4?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Description: Temple in which Doctor Strange learned the mystic arts from the Ancient One, situated in the mountains above the (fictional) village of Kamar-Taj.<br>Notes: The original origin story from Strange Tales #115 set the temple in India. Since then, accounts place it in Tibet, "high in the Himalayas." This placemark in the disputed Arunchal Province allows both settings to be kind of true, at least until more specific source material comes to light.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1594-757575-labelson</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Description">
            <value>Temple in which Doctor Strange learned the mystic arts from the Ancient One, situated in the mountains above the (fictional) village of Kamar-Taj.</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Notes">
            <value><![CDATA[The original origin story from Strange Tales #115 set the temple in India. Since then, accounts place it in Tibet, "high in the Himalayas." This placemark in the disputed Arunchal Province allows both settings to be kind of true, at least until more specific source material comes to light.]]></value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value><![CDATA[https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR7wuTm_JoK9gnQJ-HnWDUVrq5Ls--o-dksbqOoJ79jDfb2xnwYoGUytyyJUELHq_IGuBNltqXzVEws7GsLyxj-dhrjm8lx2AvRjO0y4xY5Rp8IxWGI_pdNLbY-LCHuDiyvsKldo6SCN4rfdhECT8mJhdsklzcrl2rJiGe7iyOCNgRsGG6dgPHQEmpp16sgwR1w44x4?authuser=0&fife=s16383]]></value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            95.8238802,29.0713778,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name><![CDATA[Angel's Aerie]]></name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR43xNrWfmzsYUih_ZFjfrOF7hY8RzvTYLaTOXEubBMg7UB24_QFDZHCQRZBl2-tx79MpfAZz2n8HVIlu49yjQJeZ_kEOZwZY8Ux9Tm31NqfDO-15QsRq7MwUXqs2kDSFBn0AieRY7WbvJhl53BmUSITvlE0VybLsL7sziUspMyt8tQRs5dNNC6HrIFy3gOyDrUn5sI?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Description: Warren Worthington's mountain retreat that has been used as a de facto headquarters for X-Force and the New Defenders.<br>Notes: Although more recent X-Force accounts mention a vague Colorado location, this location uses the original portrayals from the Dark Phoenix saga (Uncanny X-Men #132), Hulk Annual #7, and Marvel Fanfare #1 which specifically places it in New Mexico, within 100 miles from Gamma Base.<br>]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1594-757575-labelson</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Description">
            <value><![CDATA[Warren Worthington's mountain retreat that has been used as a de facto headquarters for X-Force and the New Defenders.]]></value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Notes">
            <value>Although more recent X-Force accounts mention a vague Colorado location, this location uses the original portrayals from the Dark Phoenix saga (Uncanny X-Men #132), Hulk Annual #7, and Marvel Fanfare #1 which specifically places it in New Mexico, within 100 miles from Gamma Base.
</value>
          </Data>
