        <name><![CDATA[Baron Zemo's WWII Nazi Base]]></name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR4GyQOF-XL3yHR0vvo-nE_XrEvUocoGj5BAfSkiM0pQIHP59qx6ND8TiyUKJV4p7ftxZlMKknV84CSfKOJybnvrJDBAx-B33nDMC-k7ApYZ9GYjibImxIO5oNouTiSTrWargZluLmFhT8-1gkhZHszmJnbB9KMJ4QpW6cUISNvO0ssm3tQ5Rm0DgfiU_cZ_qShDU9Y?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Description: Nazi-held island from which Captain America and Bucky were believed KIA after disabling an explosive drone plane<br>Notes: Ed Brubaker's Captain America (2004) #6 clarified decades of inconsistent locations by establishing this event happened on an "uncharted" Channel Island. Beyond that, this placemark is meant to be a bit out of the way of shipping lanes.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1594-757575-labelson</styleUrl>
