      <Placemark>
        <name>Camp Hammond</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR6CGrBEIUhOBbn0jcO9ENMTxvTtrO3cGXDbjf_a53Qj3jQQrpaZjt5LaefdxH5-M1lDf2x3kcnjFxjNaKGsmGDhguMUW_1z4-FSFgVUBmQCKQGE3BIgUtmZZzVBdF9Sn_FtUqtRnoAZLBdHk_pOGsSBximvzW1w65Nfz8iOtYxNzb0y1d-2f9GATwBzHBV49Y3TT8U?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Description: The superhuman training facility used by the 50-State Initiative in the wake of the Stamford tragedy and the Superhuman Registration Act<br><br>Notes: Said to be built on the site of the Stamford explosion — which occurred near an elementary school in a residential neighborhood. The Marvel Atlas notes that Camp Hammond is “located on the ‘Gold Coast’ of Connecticut’s Fairfield County and within a short drive to the Lodge Turnpike (US I-95).”]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1594-757575-labelson</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Description">
            <value>The superhuman training facility used by the 50-State Initiative in the wake of the Stamford tragedy and the Superhuman Registration Act
</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Notes">
            <value>Said to be built on the site of the Stamford explosion — which occurred near an elementary school in a residential neighborhood. The Marvel Atlas notes that Camp Hammond is “located on the ‘Gold Coast’ of Connecticut’s Fairfield County and within a short drive to the Lodge Turnpike (US I-95).”</value>
          </Data>
