      <Placemark>
        <name>Cassidy Keep</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR6Yj4omlt-7_JVbKvpF9B1lDiwRoqwdAdWD-HPwA6nKr8-6cFpU0pBwZlbbdsMZBuWqp_AOB8rkCsp5Y2fpJJlNbyYwaiSZ6B0dw6xwWdgcxPnTVNoWQGZ7l1SQ3wMxVHHs4KRjB3992iUZH6DqdoBxYF2chW23nP6I_32StfOn63kTeRwfgS6K52y4i12F69YDVR0?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Description: Ancestral home of the sonic mutant Sean Cassidy (Banshee) and his daughter Theresa<br>Notes: Located on a rocky cliffside in County Mayo. Uncanny X-Men #101 notes that as one heads west from Dublin, they detrain in Balina and continue on to the coast. Classic X-Men #16 shows Banshee crosses Donegal Bay from Northern Ireland to reach the castle, suggesting it's on the northern coast of the county.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1594-757575-labelson</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Description">
            <value>Ancestral home of the sonic mutant Sean Cassidy (Banshee) and his daughter Theresa</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Notes">
            <value><![CDATA[Located on a rocky cliffside in County Mayo. Uncanny X-Men #101 notes that as one heads west from Dublin, they detrain in Balina and continue on to the coast. Classic X-Men #16 shows Banshee crosses Donegal Bay from Northern Ireland to reach the castle, suggesting it's on the northern coast of the county.]]></value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value><![CDATA[https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR6Yj4omlt-7_JVbKvpF9B1lDiwRoqwdAdWD-HPwA6nKr8-6cFpU0pBwZlbbdsMZBuWqp_AOB8rkCsp5Y2fpJJlNbyYwaiSZ6B0dw6xwWdgcxPnTVNoWQGZ7l1SQ3wMxVHHs4KRjB3992iUZH6DqdoBxYF2chW23nP6I_32StfOn63kTeRwfgS6K52y4i12F69YDVR0?authuser=0&fife=s16383]]></value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            -9.2144668,54.2876631,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Castle Family Murders</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR7JJ-D3pf_Mq0J-m9nH5E9R_DJgOPQEB4KYuvnWWKVK4Uwp3Fe6bXIQBJhuBj6mj1ajGJlilGL_OKwEKD-Vh6SaO9pcVbx4BNfhoCjUVVEbxo2xvqBmCopIFOCTVTE2_7UKyTCcYxIvplnFt8yn6eEhDYChqxzTexuqsO5aEFuoh2RVEMxfg2vUqIBY5-9vGP__xPc?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Description: Site of the murder of Frank Castle's family after having stumbled upon a gang execution.<br>Notes: Frank’s family was killed in a Central Park broad and open enough for his son to fly his kite, yet secluded enough for a gang to execute someone in broad daylight. Punisher War Journal #1 (1988) shows Frank preparing for his memorial visit to the location from his West Side safehouse, which he says is close to Harlem. So I narrowed my focus to the upper west side of the park. As it turns out, there is a clearing almost entirely surrounded by trees that fits the description really well. Someone even created a panoramic Street View photo sphere from within the space if you view the location on Google Maps.<br>]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1594-757575-labelson</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Description">
            <value><![CDATA[Site of the murder of Frank Castle's family after having stumbled upon a gang execution.]]></value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Notes">
            <value>Frank’s family was killed in a Central Park broad and open enough for his son to fly his kite, yet secluded enough for a gang to execute someone in broad daylight. Punisher War Journal #1 (1988) shows Frank preparing for his memorial visit to the location from his West Side safehouse, which he says is close to Harlem. So I narrowed my focus to the upper west side of the park. As it turns out, there is a clearing almost entirely surrounded by trees that fits the description really well. Someone even created a panoramic Street View photo sphere from within the space if you view the location on Google Maps.
</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value><![CDATA[https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR7JJ-D3pf_Mq0J-m9nH5E9R_DJgOPQEB4KYuvnWWKVK4Uwp3Fe6bXIQBJhuBj6mj1ajGJlilGL_OKwEKD-Vh6SaO9pcVbx4BNfhoCjUVVEbxo2xvqBmCopIFOCTVTE2_7UKyTCcYxIvplnFt8yn6eEhDYChqxzTexuqsO5aEFuoh2RVEMxfg2vUqIBY5-9vGP__xPc?authuser=0&fife=s16383]]></value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            -73.957842,40.7959713,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Centerville, California</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR7KJgiXbESuAxX2EzjG7-NZKtsBAuWvrAWd6kL1egA2MAS5YGQ0D4j99tbRc9MTGAIAGaB1NuaMW79jt7FVHEP1lCkqFyb8Lj9a-4vnwKRfBOs9nd_fFJTayLITnRYgtpGRAbkeQGXIxGBDOszwbKupfRaZX17_1taPrQLg52DEcg7oM_y3k_vNhQCfhp_mZfdjkPE?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Description: Hometown of Patsy Walker, aka Hellcat<br>Notes: The real world Centerville is not as populated as its comic book counterpart, but it exists nonetheless.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1594-757575-labelson</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Description">
            <value>Hometown of Patsy Walker, aka Hellcat</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Notes">
            <value>The real world Centerville is not as populated as its comic book counterpart, but it exists nonetheless.</value>
          </Data>
