      <Placemark>
        <name>Empire State University</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR5skQZBIFt1Kf79dlG9QW8y0NUuMQ0hGKovcc0vnXab3N285lKhif7vwFno8lwMVwT3XUYil2DS27E3ItlMUjuIUIsFZS6c-xRo7zcXfGEgvI7KwxIYth0B3c5vKthrHXVFy1V0FPeo5ME6sUOH8RkcCUyTmVjVOjIo_7tAIJ-d36iX8tiRy1Cvz9lZGHJyTm_LBak?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Description: The college university attended by numerous individuals, including: Peter Parker, Reed Richards, Ben Grimm, Victor Von Doom, Emma Frost, Eddie Brock, Flash Thompson, Felicia Hardy, Kevin Conner, and Doreen Green.<br><br>Notes: It’s a little tricky reconciling the compact, walled-in ESU campus with its real-world counterpart: NYU, which has a nebulous, urban campus open to the rest of the city. Adding to the complications is that the various editions of the Official Handbooks place ESU in the East Village, closer to Tompkins Park. But it feels wrong to divorce ESU from its counterpart NYU and Washington Square Park, so the best compromise I could devise is specifying a rectangular area adjacent to Washington Square to the south, which overlaps a sufficient portion of the real world college grounds.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1594-757575-labelson</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Description">
            <value>The college university attended by numerous individuals, including: Peter Parker, Reed Richards, Ben Grimm, Victor Von Doom, Emma Frost, Eddie Brock, Flash Thompson, Felicia Hardy, Kevin Conner, and Doreen Green.
</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Notes">
            <value>It’s a little tricky reconciling the compact, walled-in ESU campus with its real-world counterpart: NYU, which has a nebulous, urban campus open to the rest of the city. Adding to the complications is that the various editions of the Official Handbooks place ESU in the East Village, closer to Tompkins Park. But it feels wrong to divorce ESU from its counterpart NYU and Washington Square Park, so the best compromise I could devise is specifying a rectangular area adjacent to Washington Square to the south, which overlaps a sufficient portion of the real world college grounds.</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value><![CDATA[https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR5skQZBIFt1Kf79dlG9QW8y0NUuMQ0hGKovcc0vnXab3N285lKhif7vwFno8lwMVwT3XUYil2DS27E3ItlMUjuIUIsFZS6c-xRo7zcXfGEgvI7KwxIYth0B3c5vKthrHXVFy1V0FPeo5ME6sUOH8RkcCUyTmVjVOjIo_7tAIJ-d36iX8tiRy1Cvz9lZGHJyTm_LBak?authuser=0&fife=s16383]]></value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            -73.9973378,40.7280819,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Fact Channel Studios</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR4tZW7cZJnu45lE7XSaFDmXyde96pJvjM5UhjyykBfJLBcnU0YSpIMmwMnNApaEOvTDkJ-fFfbuY4FVZ1DxIGaYIeMveUV_KmNxdin6Jk0odlq5z49cslI8pXz0ffOSVXy4raMfWOMVCZCD6sTjKNkadr5hJDos2gEA4Jy-rrHACYyzl9IJ_EWkPBR25Z0-F0mf1p0?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Description: Location of cable news network, where both J. Jonah Jameson and Cindy Moon (Silk) had worked.<br>Notes: Based off the original portrayal of the location, which showed the exterior of the ABC Times Square studios (though later portrayals showed a generic building in Midtown).]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1594-757575-labelson</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Description">
            <value>Location of cable news network, where both J. Jonah Jameson and Cindy Moon (Silk) had worked.</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Notes">
            <value>Based off the original portrayal of the location, which showed the exterior of the ABC Times Square studios (though later portrayals showed a generic building in Midtown).</value>
