      <Placemark>
        <name>Howlett Estate</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR6iFLPWdEUPL2gSCoiyYh6EF7v4kdNN-sXV-5JWED8jQFyrivqmEt0LfA_-D1hvDI_khZQMxHC6zTF9LN6bfygDBPlW8QjBaime6OkKxmUdnmD7QJFwiao_hhLOjvylSP_lnSqblWDeYLWRYUDvCjr9htkJZp5LcA6cyXvzRlGEfH9Phz2FzPuHCUUp4jl5QWs6Z3s?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Description: Nineteenth-century birthplace and family home of James Howlett, aka Logan / Wolverine<br>Notes: The comics portray this location as being built in the Canadian Rocky Mountains. The most telling clue in Origin #3 is when the characters flee the town into British Columbia by rail. The only rail line that went through that area at that period was the Canadian Pacific, which went through the Rocky Mountain towns of Canmore and Banff and of those two, Banff has a few qualities that suit the portrayal just enough to make this my pick. Wolverine #10 (2013) showed a shopping mall had since been built on the site so I looked for some newer hillside construction (and having a Wolverine St. just down the hill doesn't hurt either).]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1594-757575-labelson</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Description">
            <value>Nineteenth-century birthplace and family home of James Howlett, aka Logan / Wolverine</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Notes">
            <value><![CDATA[The comics portray this location as being built in the Canadian Rocky Mountains. The most telling clue in Origin #3 is when the characters flee the town into British Columbia by rail. The only rail line that went through that area at that period was the Canadian Pacific, which went through the Rocky Mountain towns of Canmore and Banff and of those two, Banff has a few qualities that suit the portrayal just enough to make this my pick. Wolverine #10 (2013) showed a shopping mall had since been built on the site so I looked for some newer hillside construction (and having a Wolverine St. just down the hill doesn't hurt either).]]></value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value><![CDATA[https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR6iFLPWdEUPL2gSCoiyYh6EF7v4kdNN-sXV-5JWED8jQFyrivqmEt0LfA_-D1hvDI_khZQMxHC6zTF9LN6bfygDBPlW8QjBaime6OkKxmUdnmD7QJFwiao_hhLOjvylSP_lnSqblWDeYLWRYUDvCjr9htkJZp5LcA6cyXvzRlGEfH9Phz2FzPuHCUUp4jl5QWs6Z3s?authuser=0&fife=s16383]]></value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            -115.562063455675,51.1723611281769,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
