      <Placemark>
        <name><![CDATA[K'un-Lun]]></name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR6EFFGg67Wqn6cvQytJv-7bxyAygoGeTa2PpA9etg5GP7z1ijngUuTMEZ_ZjYF78rLfkBNHyzULP0re_g-eWRCM3mNdyJhfqiXzEIeCerDqulb_7T8m05clLNk_Dz6LGL46NSOXG8oRxgNX5l3zOND_EwJ1O1hETMqZotIGNzwx-4a2gPA0860ndANrEydjFDHUDck?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Description: Portal to the mystical otherdimensional realm that produced the Iron Fist legacy.<br>Notes: Most old comics and the Handbooks specify this location is in the Himalayan Mountains but the most impactful recent comic (The Immortal Iron Fist) places this location in the Kunlun Mountains. I went with the Kunlun region partially because when there is a discrepancy, popular and recent comics generally tend to drive canon; and frankly, the matching names is too good to pass up.<br>]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1594-757575-labelson</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Description">
            <value>Portal to the mystical otherdimensional realm that produced the Iron Fist legacy.</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Notes">
            <value>Most old comics and the Handbooks specify this location is in the Himalayan Mountains but the most impactful recent comic (The Immortal Iron Fist) places this location in the Kunlun Mountains. I went with the Kunlun region partially because when there is a discrepancy, popular and recent comics generally tend to drive canon; and frankly, the matching names is too good to pass up.
</value>
