        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR6JU8NPt7YVsrZTGrUKsgvjxv8QMCCw-0x8PIZ3PNWO0Tgk3u-kkqRKMsKoNnvFx5h-PgnNH5czNdBR9lW9jZ6o9BRBCQ3fR0ICTzimNPNzOj3hKWGNk9FZuurg9iDEUsJK8hmdERtr2QX9BZbQUyKk4vQm4x7hC05TskqDFRrz5U0Rt2Bd3fWmh8IUPi2GS5cjVs0?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Description: Moon Knight's longtime residence and base of operations.<br>Notes: This location in Lloyd Neck reflects the location specified in the original Official Handbook, allowing the seclusion required for a “Mooncopter” to come and go without notice. A later Southampton mention from the comics is not only far too densely populated, but is also three times as far from Manhattan.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1594-757575-labelson</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Description">
            <value><![CDATA[Moon Knight's longtime residence and base of operations.]]></value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Notes">
            <value>This location in Lloyd Neck reflects the location specified in the original Official Handbook, allowing the seclusion required for a “Mooncopter” to come and go without notice. A later Southampton mention from the comics is not only far too densely populated, but is also three times as far from Manhattan.</value>
          </Data>
