      <Placemark>
        <name>Ravencroft Institute</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR5SVq_38dV6OilCBF4NA76At8LG2syaoTs9DPhrmRNHgM_TYtNQGH8Mkp7jMs-YftYLNNezTpllo3JuwxLMiJwpD3PqKN27IguAyA7bQBonmyqOA56g4G_hiKbGKQK-ZNqYeLklREj5EXtuwhPNAni-W1RUGQ6bQgTOzJ4PSoAysc4M40u0WtllXhFOE6mgNplPAoI?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Description: Maximum-security facility for the criminally insane, run by Dr. Ashley Kafka prior to her death.<br>Notes: Generally placed in Westchester County, Amazing Spider-Man went on to specify that it lay 25 miles north of New York City. The portrayal of the land in Ruins of Ravencroft: Sabretooth show it was placed on land that was never developed, alongside a river — presumably the Hudson. Given the number of times Spider-Man — who doesn't drive — visited Ravencroft, it is reasonable the location is fairly accessible via the Hudson Line.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1594-757575-labelson</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Description">
            <value>Maximum-security facility for the criminally insane, run by Dr. Ashley Kafka prior to her death.</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Notes">
            <value><![CDATA[Generally placed in Westchester County, Amazing Spider-Man went on to specify that it lay 25 miles north of New York City. The portrayal of the land in Ruins of Ravencroft: Sabretooth show it was placed on land that was never developed, alongside a river — presumably the Hudson. Given the number of times Spider-Man — who doesn't drive — visited Ravencroft, it is reasonable the location is fairly accessible via the Hudson Line.]]></value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
