      <Placemark>
        <name>Red Room</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR5qJ0F1eBQjzs-0MOHYQLjthWCy1A0neZGaUUqzvoGodwDolo20jriVs4F1vEgaJgM3RszMwxUvX9-LyYc4sRbPfz-PTZIobOOGWR3Ar-VnY1ARFxUp3pLYD-YdzQ2eREwycRg_XeZixxPvJtmHo8LS4hs5rsTwjc0IuQO_7vWyv0TWxewc0MIOP7NqAFcSeNzT0tE?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Description: Russian intelligence facility home to the Black Widow program<br>Notes: While there are numerous satellite Red Room locations (including a remote mountain location Natasha spent time at while still a child), numerous comics from 1999-2015 have based the Red Room in or just outside Moscow. 2002’s Black Widow: Pale Little Spider #1 closely associates the Red Room with the real-world GRU “Aquarium” headquarters. This placemark is dropped on a random building within the GRU complex.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1594-757575-labelson</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Description">
            <value>Russian intelligence facility home to the Black Widow program</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Notes">
            <value>While there are numerous satellite Red Room locations (including a remote mountain location Natasha spent time at while still a child), numerous comics from 1999-2015 have based the Red Room in or just outside Moscow. 2002’s Black Widow: Pale Little Spider #1 closely associates the Red Room with the real-world GRU “Aquarium” headquarters. This placemark is dropped on a random building within the GRU complex.</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
