      <Placemark>
        <name>Valley of the Spirits / Dragons</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR5zPIWoFu7VlQWJk6Thi7qG9qnQkIqRrCtOkSqNQ2wq6t5plyp10qK1MuUft0N8qD3QGQAWKk_1c85daX317nIu7ouBfOgWOZ6PyYm1LLEzuKRVlrFMW6DZeoX767fKBS3z3PHKzgid5X_HPHqE4noU4ANlEhf-2hToT76gMSVl23cX8lHxJa3N_XABTU80MQ9xKyc?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Description: The site of an ancient spacecraft crash, from which the Mandarin acquired his ten rings of power, who went on to inhabit a fortress in the valley. (not to be confused with the Valley of the Sleeping Dragon, where Fin Fang Foom was confined for ages).<br>Notes: The Mandarin grew up in Habuquan as a small-time criminal and had to flee Mao’s regime. So I looked for uninhabited mountain valleys downrange away from Beijing. This placemark is about 40 miles downrange west of Habuquan.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1594-757575-labelson</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Description">
            <value>The site of an ancient spacecraft crash, from which the Mandarin acquired his ten rings of power, who went on to inhabit a fortress in the valley. (not to be confused with the Valley of the Sleeping Dragon, where Fin Fang Foom was confined for ages).</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Notes">
            <value>The Mandarin grew up in Habuquan as a small-time criminal and had to flee Mao’s regime. So I looked for uninhabited mountain valleys downrange away from Beijing. This placemark is about 40 miles downrange west of Habuquan.</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value><![CDATA[https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR5zPIWoFu7VlQWJk6Thi7qG9qnQkIqRrCtOkSqNQ2wq6t5plyp10qK1MuUft0N8qD3QGQAWKk_1c85daX317nIu7ouBfOgWOZ6PyYm1LLEzuKRVlrFMW6DZeoX767fKBS3z3PHKzgid5X_HPHqE4noU4ANlEhf-2hToT76gMSVl23cX8lHxJa3N_XABTU80MQ9xKyc?authuser=0&fife=s16383]]></value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            111.3569058,40.8199321,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Wakanda</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR6XWkgDPDhDRekOB1Udq7grPhv6N8_8bcDeiNAkE5yT8D-NBjtgYBdm7oly6JZe1vfzLfYy_QcEB1DeivW1Jz-jOK2p4nPhfSmja6v8nH9TdB1shewb3Ty-lLL0PWiHirqTvyV83PamdiPsgPQSVRL20BHixrZKl9vdNCVSiY6NqjZCJR1YQIiVBotGJrYwI4x07rU?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Description: Black Panther’s technologically advanced nation home to the world’s supply of Vibranium.<br><br>Notes: These land borders were created by superimposing Ta-Nehisi Coates’ map of Wakanda over a real-world map and (mostly) matching the Lake Victoria shoreline and filling in the few areas that ran off the edge of the comic page. The main question is whether I got the relative size right.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1594-757575-labelson</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Description">
            <value>Black Panther’s technologically advanced nation home to the world’s supply of Vibranium.
</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Notes">
            <value>These land borders were created by superimposing Ta-Nehisi Coates’ map of Wakanda over a real-world map and (mostly) matching the Lake Victoria shoreline and filling in the few areas that ran off the edge of the comic page. The main question is whether I got the relative size right.</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value><![CDATA[https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR6XWkgDPDhDRekOB1Udq7grPhv6N8_8bcDeiNAkE5yT8D-NBjtgYBdm7oly6JZe1vfzLfYy_QcEB1DeivW1Jz-jOK2p4nPhfSmja6v8nH9TdB1shewb3Ty-lLL0PWiHirqTvyV83PamdiPsgPQSVRL20BHixrZKl9vdNCVSiY6NqjZCJR1YQIiVBotGJrYwI4x07rU?authuser=0&fife=s16383]]></value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            31.4697652,-0.9393548,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Weapon X Facility</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR4F2LaRAxaxwi6zN6ghR6eEbMqZSwaeFwGG1Wnfydhv4APB8031WkTqO6QFLX8uxCLpleHDNrGbriFFnwWVqcw4cPmQl-emKKlqLKZmSYTSH7qG9LuvWJIp5D0rKoWDFp8yGuK6vIxzVH4r-kihvcNcG9ulD_G6RFbwk4MkswQVOfD51brdnSd4utfW3vFgcsDyu6o?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Description: Facility that fused adamatium onto Wolverine's bones; later used by a faction of the X-Men as their headquarters.<br>Notes: There are precious few clues about this location beyond placing it in the Canadian Rockies. In lieu of better evidence, all we can do is note that in Uncanny X-Men #2, Bachalo uses Banff National Park’s Valley of the Ten Peaks as his backdrop for the site’s exterior.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1594-757575-labelson</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Description">
            <value><![CDATA[Facility that fused adamatium onto Wolverine's bones; later used by a faction of the X-Men as their headquarters.]]></value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Notes">
            <value>There are precious few clues about this location beyond placing it in the Canadian Rockies. In lieu of better evidence, all we can do is note that in Uncanny X-Men #2, Bachalo uses Banff National Park’s Valley of the Ten Peaks as his backdrop for the site’s exterior.</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value><![CDATA[https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR4F2LaRAxaxwi6zN6ghR6eEbMqZSwaeFwGG1Wnfydhv4APB8031WkTqO6QFLX8uxCLpleHDNrGbriFFnwWVqcw4cPmQl-emKKlqLKZmSYTSH7qG9LuvWJIp5D0rKoWDFp8yGuK6vIxzVH4r-kihvcNcG9ulD_G6RFbwk4MkswQVOfD51brdnSd4utfW3vFgcsDyu6o?authuser=0&fife=s16383]]></value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            -116.1810905,51.3278178,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>Weirdworld portal</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR5EOnRdURHKxqIIqBM1ZjGBqPXqfUayzBvRYv_blqdj1ON6WOKsoQUi14ipVkWfMkgljhsoQyrV6hiWxy9crLxHNlj3k7OQ1Rw_cXV94haFLqzflW4d681JrE3p02xh8sMYGmNNAmg9KudjK168q8olriDgJmrEPjUGPFY25mplkdiNRG7SHkbaJLAJtxnLQTEzxlA?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Description: Access point between Earth and the magical realm known as Weirdworld<br>Notes: Although references cite that the portal is in the Bermuda Triangle (which is east of Miami), Rebecca Rodriguez's flight ventured into it on a flight from Miami to Guadalajara (which is west of Miami). This placemark is placed at random along the Miami/Guadalajara flight path.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1594-757575-labelson</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Description">
            <value>Access point between Earth and the magical realm known as Weirdworld</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Notes">
            <value><![CDATA[Although references cite that the portal is in the Bermuda Triangle (which is east of Miami), Rebecca Rodriguez's flight ventured into it on a flight from Miami to Guadalajara (which is west of Miami). This placemark is placed at random along the Miami/Guadalajara flight path.]]></value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value><![CDATA[https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR5EOnRdURHKxqIIqBM1ZjGBqPXqfUayzBvRYv_blqdj1ON6WOKsoQUi14ipVkWfMkgljhsoQyrV6hiWxy9crLxHNlj3k7OQ1Rw_cXV94haFLqzflW4d681JrE3p02xh8sMYGmNNAmg9KudjK168q8olriDgJmrEPjUGPFY25mplkdiNRG7SHkbaJLAJtxnLQTEzxlA?authuser=0&fife=s16383]]></value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            -86.6227367,24.7228529,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>X-Men Mansion</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR4FdMQnz2dfJlx4cvXpy47tPdNbCDsgksbKYOXiSdirB6beMrEV-84PMv8TS6Th6h5MpYY-tC4rK3qRLvFDQi4xKLxiclSjWrMAuWDOV5szwwEGVWcMvDmXRUE3fMDiy9dYZOsxBfEmlFITAvjsfWIZmxm7gsfqn5b4obyny1YqjrcF4_swf5XC8yE5FrpzshUZJZE?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Description: Original site of the Westchester estate that was a longtime headquarters for the X-Men and school to young mutants.<br>Notes: Although the real-world hamlet of Westchester’s Salem Center is nowhere near as populated as its comic book counterpart, I can’t in good conscience place the X-Men mansion anywhere else, using the Titicus Reservoir as a stand-in for Breakstone Lake and Mills Road as the real Graymalkin Lane. Although maps of the estate traditionally position the grounds on the North Shore, the south shore’s terrain more closely reflects the fictional grounds with enough area between the lake and the road.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1594-757575-labelson</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Description">
            <value>Original site of the Westchester estate that was a longtime headquarters for the X-Men and school to young mutants.</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Notes">
            <value>Although the real-world hamlet of Westchester’s Salem Center is nowhere near as populated as its comic book counterpart, I can’t in good conscience place the X-Men mansion anywhere else, using the Titicus Reservoir as a stand-in for Breakstone Lake and Mills Road as the real Graymalkin Lane. Although maps of the estate traditionally position the grounds on the North Shore, the south shore’s terrain more closely reflects the fictional grounds with enough area between the lake and the road.</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value><![CDATA[https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR4FdMQnz2dfJlx4cvXpy47tPdNbCDsgksbKYOXiSdirB6beMrEV-84PMv8TS6Th6h5MpYY-tC4rK3qRLvFDQi4xKLxiclSjWrMAuWDOV5szwwEGVWcMvDmXRUE3fMDiy9dYZOsxBfEmlFITAvjsfWIZmxm7gsfqn5b4obyny1YqjrcF4_swf5XC8yE5FrpzshUZJZE?authuser=0&fife=s16383]]></value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            -73.618631,41.3276728,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name>X-Statix Headquarters</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR4Y7StPZT0W1vN6y3N_2achPpGo0gZjKSiNXmReHsyKaf_Ys6ct7vdSxHo49MXHiKaKr6plPzoaw9Pbc8bIVUUc0yTw2zoWkYk_DZnZAbuWtDJKe3RO_n5vW9CR8gsucvkJ8sHyNm-duXzL1iMLqk__dNYvRY9Du4RgXFcaLd8rUfA82YL63jlZQzlESJFXyFAbGcM?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Description: The former HQ of the media-savvy team of mutants.<br>Notes: The group's (fictional) converted Loyola Theater is shown to overlook the ocean, and just north of Santa Monica Pier.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1769-FF5252-labelson</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Description">
            <value>The former HQ of the media-savvy team of mutants.</value>
