      <Placemark>
        <name>Yancy Street</name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR6Tt5OAwO74omvqmYs97WvIJTSEAVyWd80MZ6nZsSGRnCZ29QL5DYuDfBNOV43FSGjJPOPq9HU0Glu3sdFhR4kCyTBqYgP2Ud2mhm7pmMA-JWasOyJZEd9mmTCODzHYJEjA7OeJxHThAIBDGEH07_xzsRCjI1rLs9w_vEbP4646PchLrXSidepfkUUC55Mmx9wUrr4?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Description: Lower East Side home of the Thing, Moon Girl and the Yancy Street Gang<br><br>Notes: Inspired in name by the real-life Lower East Side thoroughfare Delancy Street, Marvel’s Yancy Street is instead more of a side-street. Unfortunately, early representations of the street intersecting with 10th (and the non-existent 19th) Avenues take it out of the Lower East Side neighborhood it is supposed to be in. More helpfully, the map of Manhattan from the original Official Handbook indicates the street runs east-west, and later maps from the Official Handbook Deluxe Edition and the Spider-Man Encyclopedia position it just below Delancy Street / Williamsburg Bridge. The real-world Broome Street fits all these characteristics.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1594-757575-labelson</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Description">
            <value>Lower East Side home of the Thing, Moon Girl and the Yancy Street Gang
</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="Notes">
            <value>Inspired in name by the real-life Lower East Side thoroughfare Delancy Street, Marvel’s Yancy Street is instead more of a side-street. Unfortunately, early representations of the street intersecting with 10th (and the non-existent 19th) Avenues take it out of the Lower East Side neighborhood it is supposed to be in. More helpfully, the map of Manhattan from the original Official Handbook indicates the street runs east-west, and later maps from the Official Handbook Deluxe Edition and the Spider-Man Encyclopedia position it just below Delancy Street / Williamsburg Bridge. The real-world Broome Street fits all these characteristics.</value>
          </Data>
          <Data name="gx_media_links">
            <value><![CDATA[https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR6Tt5OAwO74omvqmYs97WvIJTSEAVyWd80MZ6nZsSGRnCZ29QL5DYuDfBNOV43FSGjJPOPq9HU0Glu3sdFhR4kCyTBqYgP2Ud2mhm7pmMA-JWasOyJZEd9mmTCODzHYJEjA7OeJxHThAIBDGEH07_xzsRCjI1rLs9w_vEbP4646PchLrXSidepfkUUC55Mmx9wUrr4?authuser=0&fife=s16383]]></value>
          </Data>
        </ExtendedData>
        <Point>
          <coordinates>
            -73.9886844,40.7176733,0
          </coordinates>
        </Point>
      </Placemark>
      <Placemark>
        <name><![CDATA[Savage Land & Pangea]]></name>
        <description><![CDATA[<img src="https://mymaps.usercontent.google.com/hostedimage/m/*/3AAjQbR7nPfQ48bY1Fy2UhMxHILh77z3A34nCXrbZFeOBPIPbWbYy9YV_HHuKg89z5RZ_QxTodt7D3QXn-Zc2-9h1GSUk7XuawcfB19ftStrA1a0Er0ld8gOgbsthJsX7D48AR8MK891PIB72c24Fmie9qTwBnJ36H1MaIu5KcuOumxZsdYSV7piFxg-tmHIC_W0NsUu4-1c?authuser=0&fife=s16383" height="200" width="auto" /><br><br>Description: Artificially-created tropical forest region home to a variety of semi-humanoid races and otherwise-extinct species of animals<br>Notes: The position, size, and boundaries of the Savage Land and Pangea have been fairly consistently consistent since the original Handbook.]]></description>
        <styleUrl>#icon-1769-FF5252-labelson</styleUrl>
        <ExtendedData>
          <Data name="Description">
            <value>Artificially-created tropical forest region home to a variety of semi-humanoid races and otherwise-extinct species of animals</value>
